    {
      "title": "Macron says ‘welcome back’ to Burnham suggestion UK could rejoin EU",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/30/macron-welcome-back-burnham-suggestion-uk-could-rejoin-eu",
      "description": "<p>French president, speaking alongside Spanish counterpart Pedro Sánchez, says EU bid would be good news for UK and Europeans</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/30/andy-burnham-eu-brexit-rejoin-customs-union-fuel-duty-budget-latest-news-updates\"><strong>UK politics live – latest updates</strong></a></p></li></ul><p>The French president, Emmanuel Macron, has reacted warmly to Andy Burnham’s suggestion that the UK could rejoin the EU.</p><p>“Welcome back,” the French leader said in English with a smile at a news conference in Madrid on Wednesday. Macron continued in French: “If the British want to come back and if the prime minister is moving in that direction, I think that is very good news, both for his country and for the Europeans.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/30/macron-welcome-back-burnham-suggestion-uk-could-rejoin-eu\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-30T16:40:27"
    },
